{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And you shall gather it</b> Two times in the Masorah: this one and the other ואספתו מצרעתו (and you shall gather him from his leprosy). This is what they expounded: afflictions come upon the stingy who does not want to lend his vessels and says 'I do not have,' and the next day afflictions come upon his house and the priest commands 'and they shall clear the house,' and they take out the vessels and see that he has everything. And this is ואספתו אל תוך ביתך — he gathers his vessels into his house and does not lend them; and ואספתו מצרעתו — that leprosy comes upon him. Another interpretation: one who suspects the worthy is stricken in his body. And one who lost an item — he suspects everyone, even the worthy, and is stricken in his body with leprosy. And thus when you gather the lost item into your house and return it to him, he will no longer suspect others, and you gather him from his leprosy." "<b>Until your brother seeks it</b> — meaning that he must seek his sign, that he give him a sign in it. And this is what they expounded: 'Seek' — if he is a swindler, if not. What is 'not'? By the signs upon it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:10:17.132067917Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}